/*******************************
         Site Overrides
*******************************/
.ui.icon:not(i) {
  font-size: inherit; // override stupid Semantic UI reset.
}

/*
  THE WRAPPER'S LINE HEIGHT IS THE BODY'S. prefixwrap maps `html` and `body` onto `.ui-render` itself
  (themes/_app.less), so normalize's `html { line-height: 1.15 }` in the vendored reset above and our
  base font's `line-height: 1` on `body` land on the SAME element, and the reset, compiled later, won:
  every line that inherits the wrapper's line height (Text, Title, a Row's content) was 15% taller than
  in 0.34.x, where the two were different elements and the content inherited the body's 1. Measured in
  Chromium: 16.1px for 14px text, against 14px. This comes after the reset, so it wins the same way.
  `.ui-render` is left as it is by prefixwrap.
*/
.ui-render {
  line-height: 1;
}
